		"meta": {
			"author": "Stefan Mazur",
			"category": "effect",
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 29,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "Galaxy - an effect over the clip below: a glowing, twinkling galaxy of light points, nebulae and dust lanes that turns, morphs and lets supernovae flash. All shape controls are continuous, so a timeline or the sound can morph one form into another: spiral, barred spiral, lenticular, elliptical, irregular. Clock moves everything (rotation, orbits, nebulae, twinkle); if it stops, the galaxy stops. Scale sizes everything relative to the output height. Galaxy: X and Y move it in galaxy radii (zooming keeps the point in place), Size is its diameter relative to the output height (zoom), Rotation, Aspect tilts it (1 = from above, near 0 = edge-on). Shape: Core Size and Core Aspect (share of the galaxy; a stretched core), Disc Opacity (0 = only the core, an elliptical galaxy), Arm Count (fractions grow a new arm; 0 = smooth disc), Arm Twist (winding in degrees; negative mirrors), Arm Width, Bar Size (0 = no bar), Scatter (order to chaos). Stars: Star Count (for performance), Star Size (relative to the output height), Star Twinkle, Hue Variation. Colors: Core, Arm, Nebula, Dust. Nebula: Opacity, Size. Dust: Opacity, Width (lanes at the inner edge of the arms; they also darken the clip below). Supernova: trigger (button, MIDI, beat) flashes a star with a spreading ring; Size, Life in seconds, Color. Sky: Galaxy Density, small distant galaxies over the whole surface (at most 256). Seed.",
			"displayName": "Galaxy",
			"identifier": "2192d299-a005-43b7-8b33-b96c9819ba8d",
			"licenseName": "Unlicense",
			"mail": "S.Mazur@cati-co.de",
